You may have noticed the new High Score holder is:

26357056 eit_brad-Bar-Hum-Mal-Neu died on the Astral Plane on level 20.
Killed by a server failure.

"killed by a server failure" is the new death notice for a score which the
administrators have decided to insert manually to deal with an unrecoverably
crashed game.

In this case eit_brad had had the game recorder active through the entire game
and, though the showscore option wasn't available so his score wasn't stored in
the recorder, it was possible to write a script to extract a majority of kills
(those which trigger a message beginning "You kill" or "You destroy") and
calculate the number of experience points received from killing monsters,
assuming that all monsters killed were at their base attributes.

This set of assumptions will generate a score considerably lower than the
player would have received had he #quit at that point in the game, since it
will miss some kills (and undervalue others) and completely ignores all the
other factors which contribute to the game score.  With the full recording of
the game available to us, we thus feel it is fair to credit eit_brad with a
game at this score.

Please let us know, either on the newsgroup or via email, if you disagree wiith
the decision or the exact manner of calculating the credited score (the script
and its output were posted to the newsgroup yesterday).

